counterexample:
`Context-dependent`. Intermediate logging is valid only if the intermediate layer adds critical local context (e.g., matching the database ID to the failing task) before propagating.
```rust
// Correct: Adding high-level context instead of raw duplication
fn fetch_user_data(id: u64) -> Result<User, AppError> {
    db::query_user(id).map_err(|e| {
        AppError::UserContext(format!("Failed to retrieve profile for user {}", id), e)
    })
}
